eck edit/delete, check next period. But that's a lot.\n\nLet me first focus on finding clear bugs in the three areas:\n\n1. History list: section heading missing weekday name (changed area) — clear bug.\n2. Upcoming recurring payments in history built with basic expense composable — need to find a defect: maybe missing recurrent label, or wrong date/time, or shows as regular expense. Here the upcoming one shows \"Recurrent expense — 12:00 PM\" and $20. Seems okay.\n3. Analytics savings card built from shared summary — need to find mismatch. All numbers consistent so far.\n\nLet me scrutinize #3. Hmm, \"Current savings 40%\" — after spending $60 of $100. Available $40. Ideal savings $20. But wait: \"Current savings\" should perhaps be $20 (ideal) vs actual? Hmm.\n\nAlso one possible bug: the bar/progress display. Let me compare: the donut chart pink+magenta = Groceries $40 + Rent $20, fine.\n\nHmm, wait: \"Recurring expenses $20 (20%)\" label with light gray dot, \"One-time expenses $40 (40%)\" with dark green dot. But the donut chart category chips are Groceries and Rent (by purchase reason, not category). The savings card's \"Recurring expenses\" vs \"One-time expenses\" split — $20 recurring (Rent) and $40 one-time (Groceries). That's correct.\n\nBut the budget $100. Recurring 20% + one-time 40% = 60% spent; available 40%. OK.\n\nWhat about \"Current savings 40%\"? If budget is 100 and spent 60, the \"savings\" available is 40. 40%. OK.\n\nHmm, maybe the bug is in the progress bar visual (segments). Let me measure. The bar: from x=77 to x=983. Visible: gray 77-230 (153px, 16.9%), green 230-520 (290px, 32%), gray 520-808 (288px, 31.8%), pink 808-983 (175px, 19.3%). Total 100%.\n\nInterpretation maybe: pink = ideal savings 20% ($20); green = one-time expenses 40%? But green is 32%. Hmm. Unless the bar also includes \"recurring\" as a segment hidden by same color? Actually maybe green = current savings? But current savings is 40% = $40, and green ~32%. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the bar's layout: total width includes 4 segments: 20% ? 40%? 20%? 20%? Let me estimate again with screenshot coordinates perhaps inaccurate. The green from ~230 to ~520 = 290; from 77 to 983 total 906. 290/906 = 32%. Pink 175/906 = 19.3%.\n\nMaybe the bar represents the 50/30/20 distribution with actual vs ideal overlay. E.g., 20% ideal savings marked at right (pink), needs 50% ($50) and wants 30% ($30) segments gray. Green could be... hmm.\n\nActually maybe the green segment represents one-time expenses 40% but with the bar starting at 0 offset? If green starts at 16.9% (which might be the recurring 20% gray segment ending at ~20%), green ends at 49%, length 32%. Hmm, if bars are grey for recurring 20% (0-20%), green one-time 40% (20-60%)... green would be 20%-60% = 40% of width. But observed green 17%-49%? Ends at 57%? Hmm, my pixel estimates might be off due to image scaling (the preview is 1080 wide but coordinates given for 1080? The screenshot is 1080x2400. The image displayed seems 1080 wide. The bar spans x≈77-983, yes.)\n\nGreen ends at ~520/1080 = 48%. Starts at 230/1080=21%. So green 21%-48% ≈ 27% width. Hmm.\n\nLet me zoom into the bar conceptually: gray from 77 to 230 (21%), green 230-520 (48%), gray 520-808 (75%), pink 808-983 (91%). So segments at 21%, 27%, 27%, 16% of full width? Hmm, that doesn't map cleanly to 20/40/40.\n\nHmm, maybe the bar has margins (from 77 to 983 is the track). Sequence: gray 0-21%, green 21-48%, gray 48-75%, pink 75-91%. Remaining 91-100%? It ends at 983, exactly.\n\nI wonder if the bar shows: spending progress of $60 (green 60%) against the track, with ideal savings marker at 80% (pink), and available... Hmm: green 21-48 isn't from 0.\n\nI might be over-analyzing a decorative bar. Let's move on and test data changes to find functional bugs.\n\nPlan:\nA. History list tests:\n   - Section heading weekday missing (bug).\n   - Add a new expense today, check new section heading format, ordering, totals.\n   - Delete an expense, check totals update.\n   - Edit an expense, check persisted.\n   - Rotate, check state.\n   - Check \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\" toggle behavior.\n   - Verify total and budget card consistency.\n\nB. Recurring payments tests:\n   - Add a recurring expense (e.g., $10 monthly) via entry with Recurrent toggle; see it in history (possibly upcoming); check edit, mark as paid, delete, persistence.\n   - Check that recurring entry rendered with basic expense composable shows correctly (category, amount, time).\n   - Check next period behavior.\n\nC. Analytics tests:\n   - Trend/Categories tabs.\n   - Days/Week/Biweek/Total.\n   - Calendar navigation (Previous/Next), tapping a day.\n   - Savings card numbers consistency after change.\n   - Past periods.\n   - Rotate.\n\nLet's be efficient but thorough.\n\nFirst, let me verify the section heading is supposed to include weekday by checking analytics calendar heading \"Saturday, November 14\" (which includes weekday). The history heading \"13 November\" lacks it. That's the changed area so report.\n\nActually wait — maybe the section heading is \"13 November\" because the formatter produced \"EEEE, d MMMM\" but locale... No, it's missing.\n\nLet me also verify whether the section heading for the current day would show \"Today\" instead. Not needed.\n\nLet me file the first bug now? Better to reproduce once more — I already saw it twice (collapsed and expanded). Let me collect element ref. Latest observe? After screenshot, need observe. The heading element [9]. I'll file with observed_quote \"13 November\".\n\nBut hold on: maybe the expected heading is \"Friday, 13 November\" — let me confirm 13 Nov 2026 is Friday. Nov 14 2026 is Saturday, so Nov 13 is Friday. Good.\n\nLet me file this report."}
