ifferent source, now from summary. A likely introduced bug is inconsistency between the card and the rest of the app. Let me compare numbers:\n- Total Spent: $65\n- Available: 35%\n- Recurring $0 (0%) + One-time $65 (65%) = 65%. Consistent.\n- Ideal savings $20.\n\nEverything consistent. Hmm.\n\nBut hold on: \"One-time expenses $65 (65%)\" — but $65 includes the $5 Coffee + $40 Groceries + $20 Rent. After rent paid, it's classified one-time. Fine-ish.\n\nMaybe the bug is the \"Current savings 35%\" vs \"Available: $35\". Both consistent.\n\nHmm. Maybe the savings card bug is that it uses the *whole budget period* summary rather than the selected day/week. E.g., if you select Days/Week view, the Total Spent changes to the selected day's spend, but the savings card still shows period-wide numbers. Let's test: select a day (e.g., 13 Nov) and see if Total Spent changes to $40 while the savings card stays $65/$35 — inconsistent. But arguably the savings card is period-based always. Hmm.\n\nWait, the \"shared summary data\" change might mean the card should use the same summary as the top \"Total Spent\" - and if the top changes with the selected range, the card should too. Let's test Week/Biweek/Total and day selection.\n\nLet me tap \"13\" in the calendar? Currently the calendar isn't visible (scrolled). Let me scroll up to the top and interact.\n\nBut first, let me note the current state and check the Categories tab too.\n\nActually, let me scroll up to top (distance 0.8) then test tabs."}
