as category? Hmm.\n\nWait, let's revisit my expense entry flow: I tapped element 9 (the \"5\" key). Then the screen showed amount $5 and chips Transport, Food, Category. I tapped the \"Food\" chip, then a text field appeared prefilled \"Food\" and I typed \"Coffee\" and submitted. So maybe that text field was the \"category\" input (save categories on their own feature?) and by typing Coffee I created a new category \"Coffee\" instead of assigning Food category. Hmm! The \"Category\" chip appears at the end for creating a new category. Tapping \"Food\" chip might have selected Food... but then a text field appeared pre-filled \"Food\" — maybe that's the reason input for category Food, and typing \"Coffee\" set the reason to Coffee while category remained Food. Then the Categories legend should show Food.\n\nAlternatively the app's \"Categories\" analytics might group by \"Purchase Reason\" labeled as categories? Hmm.\n\nThis is getting deep. The primary changed areas are analytics savings card, recurring upcoming entries, and history section headings. The Categories tab is part of analytics screen but not specifically changed. Still, consistency is part of testing.\n\nLet me not go too deep. Priority: find bugs in the changed areas.\n\nLet me reconsider the history section heading: Developer said couldn't reproduce. Maybe the actual bug is different: the section heading is \"13 November\" but should include weekday \"Friday, 13 November\". Yet dev can't repro. Perhaps the dev expects that the heading for \"Today\" is \"Today\" and for other dates includes weekday, but their build only shows weekday if the date is not yesterday? Or maybe the heading element is generated from a shared function and the issue is that \"13 November\" is being parsed incorrectly...\n\nWait, maybe I misread: the heading \"13 November\" — maybe the weekday IS there but in a separate line/clipped? Screenshot clearly shows only \"13 November\". Hmm.\n\nMaybe the developer's \"could not reproduce\" means this is a different bug than the changed one; maybe the changed behavior is in a different section, like \"past transactions\" or \"past periods\". Let me check \"Past periods\" — maybe that's where the history date sections with weekday are. Also \"Show past transactions\" is enabled in extra features. Maybe the history list in main screen includes past transactions.\n\nHmm, \"Expense history date sections\" definitely refers to the list sections like \"13 November\". \n\nCould it be that the weekday name IS missing only for the \"13 November\" heading because of the locale/format bug, and the dev's test data had a different date? They'd see e.g. \"Friday, 13 November\" in their data? My report steps maybe too vague (\"open history list (swipe the bottom sheet into the history position)\"). They may not have known how to get there. Let me refine and re-file with exact tap/gesture steps and quote. But the instruction says \"Reproduce a problem once before you report it\" — done multiple times. Re-filing same bug with better steps is reasonable.\n\nHowever, before re-filing, let me check whether there's a weekday shown in the section heading under different conditions, e.g., when the section is for a date not \"yesterday\". I could add an expense on 11 Nov (2 days ago) to see heading format. If that shows \"Wednesday, 11 November\", then 13 Nov missing weekday might be due to it being yesterday (expected \"Yesterday\"?). Hmm.\n\nActually! Maybe the section heading for 13 November should be \"Yesterday\" (since it's yesterday) and \"Today\" for today. The changed build might format headings with weekday for older dates, while special-casing today/yesterday. But the observed \"13 November\" is neither \"Yesterday\" nor \"Friday, 13 November\". Hmm, maybe the intended heading for yesterday is just the date without weekday? Unclear.\n\nLet me look for documentation within the app — maybe Settings > Reset tutorial shows gesture hints, or there's an \"About\". Hmm.\n\nAlternative approach: check \"Past periods\" to see date sections format there. If past periods list shows e.g. \"11 Nov – 04 Dec\", not relevant.\n\nLet me check the savings card change more.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the \"analytics savings card\" change: \"the card is now built from the shared summary data.\" Maybe the expected card includes \"Recurring expenses\" percentage computed from the summary. After marking Rent paid, recurring became 0%, which seems like data loss of the recurring nature. But that might be the bug introduced: \"shared summary data\" might only include paid transactions, so the recurring total is based on upcoming recurring expenses that are not part of summary. Hmm.\n\nActually, before I marked Rent as paid, the savings card showed Recurring $20 (20%), One-time $40 (40%). The summary: recurring = upcoming unpaid Rent ($20), one-time = Groceries ($40). After Mark as paid, Rent becomes a normal transaction (one-time) so recurring = $0. The card is consistent with the summary data. Maybe that's intended behavior of \"Mark as paid\".\n\nHmm. But is it correct that \"One-time expenses\" includes a recurring expense's paid occurrence? Semantically after payment it's still a recurring expense occurrence. But whatever.\n\nLet me look for a clearer inconsistency: the \"Ideal savings: $20\" = 20% of budget. The \"Current savings 35%\" = available 35. But \"If you save the 20% each period for about 6 months, you could build: $20 × 6 = $120\". Fine.\n\nMaybe the bug: the \"Current savings\" value uses available budget, which is not savings at all. But that's design, not a clear bug.\n\nLet me test the \"Total\" tab with different date selection to see if savings card numbers change with the summary. Since the card is page-level, it might reflect selected range. Let me tap a day in the calendar (e.g., 13) in Total/Categories view and see Total Spent change to $40, then check savings card (does it still show 65/35?). If the card is 