rd built from shared summary data: probably the card shows wrong values, e.g., \"Current savings\" uses the budget total instead of available, or \"Recurring expenses\" percentage is computed against spent instead of budget. Let me verify the math precisely with the current data:\n   - Budget $100, spent $75? Let's recalc: Groceries 40 + Rent 20 + Coffee 5 + Gym 10 + GymSub 3 = 78. Wait Today total $38 (Rent 20 + Coffee 5 + Gym 10 + GymSub 3 = 38) + 13 Nov $40 = $78. So total spent $78, available $22 (22%).\n   - Savings card: \"Current savings\" should be 22%. \"Available: $22\". \"Ideal savings: $20\". \"Recurring expenses\" — what should it be? GymSub $3 + next Rent $20 outside period? Hmm. Let's check the card now.\n\nLet me go to analytics and check. But first note the savings card previously: with $65 spent, recurring $0, one-time $65. That was after marking Rent paid. Before marking (spent 60), recurring $20, one-time $40.\n\nNow with spent $78 but no recurring payments marked paid (GymSub pending, Rent already paid→one-time), what does the card show? Recurring should be $3 (GymSub) maybe plus $20? Let me check.\n\nActually, let's look at the analytics \"Recurrent Expense\" count card too.\n\nLet me go to analytics. First collapse the expanded item maybe not needed. Press back to keypad, then Analytics.\n\nActually the history list has an expanded item; pressing back goes to keypad entry. Fine.\n\nLet me do it."}
