 What if the section heading is supposed to be formatted with the weekday name of the *section's date*, but the app currently shows the day/month of the *first expense's* date? E.g., the \"13 November\" heading might be showing \"13 November\" but the actual section contains expenses from 13 Nov—correct.\n\nHmm.\n\nLet me look at the heading from the accessibility tree again: \"View contains 'Collapse' | '13 November'\". The first string \"Collapse\" is the contentDescription of the toggle. What if the visible heading has more text including the weekday but the element's text extraction merges only \"13 November\"? The screenshot shows only \"13 November\". So no.\n\nOK, moving on. I have one potentially real bug (undo recurring delete) and two rejected reports. Let me try to find more clear bugs in the three areas.\n\nIdea: Check the savings card when the budget is exceeded (spent > budget). Under the \"shared summary data\", \"Available\" would be negative or 0. The card might show a negative \"Current savings\" or a broken percentage. That's a boundary test. Let me add a large expense ($50) to exceed budget (current spent 78; add 50 → 128). Then check:\n- Budget sheet: Spent $128, Available: 0%? \n- Savings card: Current savings maybe -28%? Available: $-28? Ideal $20. One-time $128 (128%). \nThat could reveal a bug (e.g., negative percent displayed as -28% or 0). Hmm, but is that in the changed area? The savings card built from shared summary could mishandle over-budget.\n\nLet me test. But adding $50 will require cleanup. I can delete it afterward. Let's do it.\n\nActually, before that, let me check the *budget sheet* current state for comparison: total spent 78, available 22%. Let me note.\n\nSteps: keypad (back from history), enter 50, category, submit. Then check analytics savings card.\n\nActually, an easier boundary: rotate device, then check. Already did.\n\nLet me proceed with the over-budget test. From history, press BACK to keypad."}
