{"type": "text", "text": "I lost the device connection partway through the sweep (`BrokenPipeError` on every device call), so I can no longer observe, tap, or file reports. Here is the state of the sweep as far as I got.\n\n## What I covered\n\n**Expense history list**\n- Budget card, date sections, per-day totals, collapse/expand, entry expand/edit/delete, undo snackbar, \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\" toggle, state after leaving/returning, rotation.\n- Verified totals against the budget sheet and analytics: seeded period (11 Nov–04 Dec, $100) with Groceries $40 and Rent $20 → $60 spent / 40% available was consistent everywhere.\n- Added/moved/deleted test expenses and watched section totals and analytics update consistently.\n\n**Recurring payments**\n- Created recurring expenses (monthly/weekly/biweekly dialog, previous/next day, limit date), edited an upcoming occurrence's amount, Mark as paid, Skip, Delete, and the Subscriptions screen (Monthly commitment, budget %, whole-period/weekly/category tabs, Due soon / Upcoming, next due dates).\n- `Mark as paid` moved the occurrence into Today and reclassified it as one-time; Skip advanced the due date; totals stayed internally consistent.\n\n**Analytics**\n- Total Spent, Trend/Categories, Days/Week/Biweek/Total, day selection, min/max/daily average, stats, category donut, and the savings card.\n- Changed savings preference between Balanced and Aggressive saver, and set/cleared a savings goal: the card's method text, \"$ × 6\", Ideal savings and Available values all updated correctly and stayed consistent with the budget summary, including the over-budget (0% available) boundary.\n- Rotated the device; analytics state (values, selected day) survived.\n\n## Issues found (filed, but developer replied \"could not reproduce\")\n\n1. **History date-section headings lack the weekday name** despite this build's change note. Repeatedly observed e.g. `13 November` and `12 November` while the app's own date picker shows \"Friday, November 13, 2026\" / \"Thursday, November 12, 2026\". Filed 3× with element refs and quotes.\n2. **Upcoming recurring payments in the history's \"subscriptions outside of the period\" section show only a time-of-day, no due date.** E.g. `Recurrent expense — 12:00 PM` for Rent while the Subscriptions screen says \"In 4 weeks (Dec 13)\"; SkipTest/GymSub are due Dec 14. Filed once.\n\n## Unfiled finding (connection died before I could log it)\n\n3. **UNDO after deleting an upcoming recurring payment does nothing.** Deleting a recurring entry from the history showed a \"`<name> deleted`\" snackbar with UNDO, but tapping UNDO did not restore it (today total stayed at $33 instead of returning to $34/$37 and the entry stayed gone). Reproduced twice (EditTest and UndoTest). A control test deleting the normal Coffee expense and tapping UNDO restored it correctly, so the failure looked specific to recurring entries.\n\nBecause of items 1–3 I do not believe the swept areas are clean, so I am not signing off. The device connection needs to be restored to finish verifying the remaining checks and to file the UNDO defect properly."}
